{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.13.15","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":21140772},{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":21143181}],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"source":"<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/arbazdevhive/rag-retrieval-benchmark?scriptVersionId=361512128\" target=\"_blank\"><img align=\"left\" alt=\"Kaggle\" title=\"Open in Kaggle\" src=\"https://kaggle.com/static/images/open-in-kaggle.svg\"></a>","metadata":{},"cell_type":"markdown"},{"id":"title","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Benchmarking Hybrid Retrieval, Neural Reranking, and Chunking Strategies for Faithful Retrieval-Augmented Generation\n\nThis is the executable Kaggle orchestration notebook for the accompanying reproducible research package. Run the cells in order: it bootstraps the attached project when necessary, runs a small smoke test first, then attempts the full resumable benchmark, and creates a verified archive in `/kaggle/working`.\n\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"section-01-markdown","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 1 — Environment setup, bootstrap, and safe recovery\n\nThe cell below checks the Kaggle hardware and Python environment, detects internet availability, establishes deterministic seeds and logging, and places the project under `/kaggle/working`. If source files are not already present, it safely locates a supplied project ZIP and extracts only a path-safe copy. Missing compatible packages are installed from the project requirements only when internet is available; the notebook does not force upgrades.","metadata":{}},{"id":"kaggle-input-fix-markdown","cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Kaggle input required\n\nBefore running the bootstrap cell, use **Add Input** in the notebook sidebar and attach **Your Datasets → `rag-zip`**. Kaggle can mount this input directly at `/kaggle/input/rag-zip/` or within its nested input layout at `/kaggle/input/datasets/arbazdevhive/rag-zip/`. This dataset supplies the project folder `RAG_Retrieval_Benchmark_Research`, rather than requiring a ZIP at one hard-coded path.\n\nThe preflight and bootstrap cells below discover a folder containing both `src/rag_benchmark` and `configs/benchmark_config.json` at any mounted depth, then fall back to a compatible ZIP if one is supplied. If the dataset is still missing, they print a concise inventory of the files Kaggle actually mounted.","metadata":{}},{"id":"kaggle-input-preflight","cell_type":"code","source":"# Kaggle input preflight — run this after attaching the rag-zip dataset.\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nKAGGLE_INPUT_ROOT = Path('/kaggle/input')\nKAGGLE_INPUT_SLUG = 'rag-zip'\nKAGGLE_PROJECT_NAME = 'RAG_Retrieval_Benchmark_Research'\n\ndef looks_like_project(path: Path) -> bool:\n    return (path / 'src' / 'rag_benchmark').is_dir() and (path / 'configs' / 'benchmark_config.json').is_file()\n\ndef find_project_source(root: Path):\n    preferred = (\n        root / KAGGLE_INPUT_SLUG / KAGGLE_PROJECT_NAME,\n        root / 'datasets' / 'arbazdevhive' / KAGGLE_INPUT_SLUG / KAGGLE_PROJECT_NAME,\n    )\n    for candidate in preferred:\n        if looks_like_project(candidate):\n            return candidate\n    try:\n        return next(\n            (config.parent.parent for config in root.rglob('benchmark_config.json')\n             if config.parent.name == 'configs' and looks_like_project(config.parent.parent)),\n            None,\n        )\n    except OSError:\n        return None\n\nif Path('/kaggle').exists():\n    source_project = find_project_source(KAGGLE_INPUT_ROOT)\n    if source_project is not None:\n        print(f'Found project folder: {source_project}')\n    else:\n        mounted_files = sorted(str(path.relative_to(KAGGLE_INPUT_ROOT)) for path in KAGGLE_INPUT_ROOT.rglob('*') if path.is_file())\n        print('Project folder is not mounted yet. Use Add Input → Your Datasets → rag-zip.')\n        print('The search checks direct and nested Kaggle input layouts recursively.')\n        print(f'Mounted files (first 50): {mounted_files[:50]}')\nelse:\n    print('Local run detected; Kaggle input preflight skipped.')","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-23T15:55:13.876982Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-23T15:55:13.877156Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-23T15:55:14.535826Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-23T15:55:13.877138Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-23T15:55:14.535033Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Found project folder: /kaggle/input/datasets/arbazdevhive/rag-zip/RAG_Retrieval_Benchmark_Research\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":1},{"id":"section-01-code","cell_type":"code","source":"from __future__ import annotations\n\nimport csv\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport socket\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nimport time\nimport traceback\nimport zipfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nPROJECT_NAME = 'RAG_Retrieval_Benchmark_Research'\nIS_KAGGLE = Path('/kaggle').exists()\nWORKING_DIR = Path('/kaggle/working') if IS_KAGGLE else Path.cwd() / 'working'\nINPUT_DIR = Path('/kaggle/input') if IS_KAGGLE else Path.cwd()\nWORKING_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nPROJECT_ROOT = WORKING_DIR / PROJECT_NAME\nARCHIVE_PATH = WORKING_DIR / 'RAG_Retrieval_Benchmark_Complete_Research.zip'\n\ndef looks_like_project(path: Path) -> bool:\n    return (path / 'src' / 'rag_benchmark').is_dir() and (path / 'configs' / 'benchmark_config.json').is_file()\n\ndef project_candidates():\n    \"\"\"Yield valid project roots, including nested Kaggle input mounts.\"\"\"\n    bases = [Path.cwd(), Path.cwd() / 'work', INPUT_DIR, WORKING_DIR]\n    seen = set()\n    for base in bases:\n        if not base.exists():\n            continue\n        candidates = [base, base / PROJECT_NAME]\n        try:\n            candidates.extend(\n                config.parent.parent\n                for config in base.rglob('benchmark_config.json')\n                if config.parent.name == 'configs'\n            )\n        except OSError:\n            pass\n        for candidate in candidates:\n            try:\n                resolved = candidate.resolve()\n            except OSError:\n                continue\n            if resolved not in seen:\n                seen.add(resolved)\n                yield candidate\n\ndef archive_candidates():\n    \"\"\"Yield likely Kaggle archives first, then ZIPs at any mounted depth.\"\"\"\n    seen = set()\n    archive_name = 'RAG_Retrieval_Benchmark_Complete_Research.zip'\n    candidates = [\n        INPUT_DIR / 'rag-zip' / archive_name,\n        INPUT_DIR / 'datasets' / 'arbazdevhive' / 'rag-zip' / archive_name,\n    ]\n    for base in (INPUT_DIR, Path.cwd()):\n        if not base.exists():\n            continue\n        try:\n            candidates.extend(base.rglob('*.zip'))\n        except OSError:\n            continue\n    for candidate in candidates:\n        try:\n            resolved = candidate.resolve()\n        except OSError:\n            continue\n        if resolved not in seen and candidate.is_file():\n            seen.add(resolved)\n            yield candidate\n\ndef archive_contains_project(archive: Path) -> bool:\n    try:\n        with zipfile.ZipFile(archive) as probe:\n            return any(name.endswith('src/rag_benchmark/__init__.py') for name in probe.namelist())\n    except (OSError, zipfile.BadZipFile):\n        return False\n\ndef safe_extract(archive: Path, destination: Path) -> None:\n    destination.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    root = destination.resolve()\n    with zipfile.ZipFile(archive) as bundle:\n        for item in bundle.infolist():\n            target = (destination / item.filename).resolve()\n            if target != root and root not in target.parents:\n                raise RuntimeError(f'Unsafe archive member rejected: {item.filename!r}')\n        bundle.extractall(destination)\n\nif not looks_like_project(PROJECT_ROOT):\n    source_root = next((item for item in project_candidates() if looks_like_project(item) and item.resolve() != PROJECT_ROOT.resolve()), None)\n    if source_root is not None:\n        print(f'Bootstrapping project from directory: {source_root}')\n        shutil.copytree(source_root, PROJECT_ROOT, dirs_exist_ok=True)\n    else:\n        selected_archive = next((candidate for candidate in archive_candidates() if archive_contains_project(candidate)), None)\n        if selected_archive is None:\n            try:\n                mounted_files = sorted(str(path.relative_to(INPUT_DIR)) for path in INPUT_DIR.rglob('*') if path.is_file())\n            except OSError:\n                mounted_files = []\n            raise FileNotFoundError(\n                'Project source was not found under /kaggle/input. Attach Your Datasets → rag-zip with Add Input; '\n                'the notebook searches recursively for a folder containing src/rag_benchmark and '\n                f'configs/benchmark_config.json. Mounted files (first 50): {mounted_files[:50]}'\n            )\n        print(f'Bootstrapping project from archive: {selected_archive.name}')\n        with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(dir=WORKING_DIR) as temporary:\n            staging = Path(temporary)\n            safe_extract(selected_archive, staging)\n            roots = [item.parent.parent for item in staging.rglob('rag_benchmark') if item.is_dir() and item.parent.name == 'src']\n            source_root = next((item for item in roots if looks_like_project(item)), None)\n            if source_root is None:\n                raise FileNotFoundError('The attached ZIP does not contain the expected src/rag_benchmark package and configuration.')\n            shutil.copytree(source_root, PROJECT_ROOT, dirs_exist_ok=True)\n\nif not looks_like_project(PROJECT_ROOT):\n    raise RuntimeError(f'Bootstrap did not produce a valid project at {PROJECT_ROOT}')\n\nfor relative in ('results/logs', 'results/tables', 'results/figures', 'cache', 'data'):\n    (PROJECT_ROOT / relative).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nos.environ.setdefault('TOKENIZERS_PARALLELISM', 'false')\nos.environ.setdefault('TRANSFORMERS_CACHE', str((Path('/kaggle/temp') if IS_KAGGLE else PROJECT_ROOT / 'cache') / 'hf_cache'))\nsys.path.insert(0, str(PROJECT_ROOT / 'src'))\n\ndef internet_available() -> bool:\n    try:\n        with socket.create_connection(('huggingface.co', 443), timeout=3):\n            return True\n    except OSError:\n        return False\n\nREQUIRED_MODULES = {\n    'numpy': 'numpy', 'pandas': 'pandas', 'matplotlib': 'matplotlib',\n    'rank_bm25': 'rank_bm25', 'sentence_transformers': 'sentence-transformers',\n    'transformers': 'transformers', 'beir': 'beir', 'datasets': 'datasets',\n    'sentencepiece': 'sentencepiece', 'psutil': 'psutil', 'tabulate': 'tabulate'\n}\nmissing = {name: package for name, package in REQUIRED_MODULES.items() if importlib.util.find_spec(name) is None}\nONLINE = internet_available()\nif missing:\n    print(f'Missing optional benchmark dependencies: {sorted(missing)}')\n    if ONLINE:\n        requirements = PROJECT_ROOT / 'requirements.txt'\n        install = subprocess.run([sys.executable, '-m', 'pip', 'install', '--disable-pip-version-check', '--no-input', '-r', str(requirements)], text=True, capture_output=True)\n        print(f'Dependency recovery return code: {install.returncode}')\n        if install.returncode:\n            print(install.stderr[-4000:])\n    else:\n        print('Internet is unavailable; the pipeline will use locally installed packages/caches when possible and record unavailable stages.')\n\nfrom rag_benchmark.environment import collect_environment, write_environment_report\nfrom rag_benchmark.pipeline import BenchmarkPipeline\nBenchmarkPipeline.reset_session_deadline(PROJECT_ROOT)\nfrom rag_benchmark.utils import atomic_write_json, set_reproducible_seed\n\nset_reproducible_seed(20261023)\nENVIRONMENT = collect_environment()\nENVIRONMENT['notebook_online_probe'] = ONLINE\nENVIRONMENT['project_root'] = str(PROJECT_ROOT)\nwrite_environment_report(PROJECT_ROOT / 'results' / 'logs' / 'environment.json')\nprint(json.dumps(ENVIRONMENT, indent=2, default=str))\n\nSTAGE_HISTORY = []\nSTAGE_STATUS_PATH = PROJECT_ROOT / 'results' / 'logs' / 'notebook_stage_status.json'\n\ndef persist_stage_history() -> None:\n    atomic_write_json(STAGE_STATUS_PATH, STAGE_HISTORY)\n\ndef run_stage(name, callback):\n    started = time.time()\n    print(f'\\n--- {name} ---')\n    try:\n        value = callback()\n        record = {'stage': name, 'status': 'completed', 'started_at_unix': started, 'runtime_seconds': round(time.time() - started, 3), 'result_type': type(value).__name__}\n        print('{}: completed in {} s'.format(name, record['runtime_seconds']))\n    except Exception as exc:\n        record = {'stage': name, 'status': 'failed', 'started_at_unix': started, 'runtime_seconds': round(time.time() - started, 3), 'error_type': type(exc).__name__, 'error': str(exc), 'traceback': traceback.format_exc(limit=4)}\n        value = None\n        print(f'{name}: failed; continuing with auditable partial outputs. {type(exc).__name__}: {exc}')\n    STAGE_HISTORY.append(record)\n    persist_stage_history()\n    return {'ok': record['status'] == 'completed', 'value': value, 'record': record}\n\ndef skip_stage(name, reason):\n    record = {'stage': name, 'status': 'skipped', 'reason': reason, 'started_at_unix': time.time(), 'runtime_seconds': 0.0}\n    STAGE_HISTORY.append(record)\n    persist_stage_history()\n    print(f'{name}: skipped — {reason}')\n    return {'ok': False, 'value': None, 'record': record}\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-23T15:55:14.538076Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-23T15:55:14.538476Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-23T15:56:20.831989Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-23T15:55:14.538448Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-23T15:56:20.831332Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Bootstrapping project from directory: /kaggle/input/datasets/arbazdevhive/rag-retrieval-benchmark-kaggle-input/RAG_Retrieval_Benchmark_Research\nMissing optional benchmark dependencies: ['beir', 'rank_bm25']\nDependency recovery return code: 0\n","output_type":"stream"},{"name":"stderr","text":"/usr/local/lib/python3.13/dist-packages/transformers/utils/hub.py:110: FutureWarning: Using `TRANSFORMERS_CACHE` is deprecated and will be removed in v5 of Transformers. Use `HF_HOME` instead.\n  warnings.warn(\n","output_type":"stream"},{"name":"stdout","text":"{\n  \"captured_at_utc\": \"2026-10-23T15:55:50Z\",\n  \"python\": \"3.13.15 (main, Aug  6 2026, 11:06:22) [GCC 13.3.0]\",\n  \"platform\": \"Linux-6.18.48+-x86_64-with-glibc2.39\",\n  \"packages\": {\n    \"torch\": \"2.11.0+cu128\",\n    \"transformers\": \"4.57.6\",\n    \"sentence_transformers\": \"3.4.1\",\n    \"beir\": \"installed (version unavailable)\",\n    \"rank_bm25\": \"installed (version unavailable)\",\n    \"faiss\": null,\n    \"psutil\": \"5.9.5\"\n  },\n  \"internet_to_huggingface\": true,\n  \"cuda\": {\n    \"available\": true,\n    \"device_count\": 2,\n    \"torch_cuda_version\": \"12.8\",\n    \"devices\": [\n      {\n        \"index\": 0,\n        \"name\": \"Tesla T4\",\n        \"total_vram_bytes\": 15636037632\n      },\n      {\n        \"index\": 1,\n        \"name\": \"Tesla T4\",\n        \"total_vram_bytes\": 15636037632\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"system_memory\": {\n    \"total_bytes\": 33658318848,\n    \"available_bytes\": 31370096640\n  },\n  \"working_disk\": {\n    \"total_bytes\": 20957446144,\n    \"free_bytes\": 20939735040\n  },\n  \"to